{% set local_problem %}
<p>Cullman's established neighborhoods feature mature trees that produce significant debris. Pine needles accumulate throughout the year. Oak and maple leaves fall heavily in autumn. Seeds and pollen add to spring accumulation. Without regular cleaning, this debris clogs gutters and prevents proper water flow.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, water overflows. In North Alabama's 55+ inches of annual rainfall, that's a lot of water going where it shouldn't — pooling around foundations, soaking into fascia boards, and eroding carefully maintained landscaping.</p>

<p>For homeowners who maintain their properties to Cullman's standards, clogged gutters undermine that care. Regular professional cleaning ensures your gutters function properly and your home stays protected.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our cleaning service is thorough, not rushed. We hand-remove all debris from inside your gutters — not just blow it onto your lawn or push it toward downspouts. Every inch gets cleaned.</p>

<p>We flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are common and often missed — we check each one.</p>

<p>While we're up there, we inspect your entire gutter system: checking hangers for looseness, looking for leaks or damage, and assessing fascia condition. If we find issues, we'll tell you. If everything looks good, we'll tell you that too.</p>

<p>When we leave, your gutters are clean, your downspouts flow freely, and all debris is removed from your property.</p>
{% endset %}

